WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.310 --> 00:00:02.190
- BoJack, what are you
trying to accomplish here?

00:00:02.190 --> 00:00:04.050
- I don't wanna do the show.

00:00:04.050 --> 00:00:05.950
- So you're gonna run
away like you always do.

00:00:05.950 --> 00:00:07.990
- Yeah, I never wanted to do this show.

00:00:07.990 --> 00:00:09.360
You faked my signature.

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:11.176
- And I told you that and you said okay

00:00:11.176 --> 00:00:13.560
because you wanted to
be a good friend to me.

00:00:13.560 --> 00:00:15.080
So you can't get points for that

00:00:15.080 --> 00:00:16.580
and then resent me for it now.

00:00:16.580 --> 00:00:17.450
- It's not about you.

00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:18.430
I don't like him.

00:00:18.430 --> 00:00:19.780
- Oh, Flip's not that bad.

00:00:19.780 --> 00:00:22.450
He's just insecure and he's
overcompensating a little.

00:00:22.450 --> 00:00:24.440
I know that must be a
foreign concept for you.

00:00:24.440 --> 00:00:26.420
- No, not Flip, Philbert.

00:00:26.420 --> 00:00:28.410
He's a drunk, he's an asshole.

00:00:28.410 --> 00:00:30.303
I don't wanna be him.

00:00:30.303 --> 00:00:32.750
- So maybe you don't be the drunk asshole.

00:00:32.750 --> 00:00:35.080
Maybe this time you have a good attitude

00:00:35.080 --> 00:00:36.440
and you don't drink so much

00:00:36.440 --> 00:00:38.090
and you show up at your call time,

00:00:38.090 --> 00:00:39.970
and then you put on the Philbert costume

00:00:39.970 --> 00:00:43.080
and you pretend to be this other guy.

00:00:43.080 --> 00:00:44.640
And then, when you're done shooting,

00:00:44.640 --> 00:00:47.800
you take off your costume
and you're BoJack,

00:00:47.800 --> 00:00:50.030
the star of the show that everybody likes.

00:00:50.030 --> 00:00:51.760
- Yeah?
- Yeah.

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:54.290
- Hey, why are we at an adoption agency?

00:00:54.290 --> 00:00:56.050
Are you adopting something?

00:00:56.050 --> 00:00:57.012
- I'm trying to.

00:00:57.012 --> 00:00:57.845
- Oh.

00:00:57.845 --> 00:01:00.790
- So, can you keep it
together for the next 10 weeks

00:01:00.790 --> 00:01:03.600
so I don't need to come to set
every day to put out fires?

00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:05.170
You think you could do that?

00:01:05.170 --> 00:01:06.662
For me?

00:01:06.662 --> 00:01:09.003
(wistful music)

00:01:09.003 --> 00:01:11.836
(breathes deeply)

00:01:13.090 --> 00:01:14.090
- [Flip] Action.

00:01:14.090 --> 00:01:15.000
- Wait, Gina.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:16.240
Can I ask you a question?

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:17.073
About you?

00:01:17.073 --> 00:01:17.960
- Uh-huh.

00:01:17.960 --> 00:01:19.710
- Do you think I'm right

00:01:19.710 --> 00:01:21.560
and the Philbert character
is poorly written

00:01:21.560 --> 00:01:22.820
and Flip needs to write him better

00:01:22.820 --> 00:01:23.920
so that I don't look so bad?

00:01:23.920 --> 00:01:26.250
- Look, I do one of these shows every year

00:01:26.250 --> 00:01:28.080
and I keep getting
hired because I show up,

00:01:28.080 --> 00:01:29.650
do the work, and keep my head down.

00:01:29.650 --> 00:01:31.030
- But do you love this script?

00:01:31.030 --> 00:01:32.490
Do you love your character?
I mean--

00:01:32.490 --> 00:01:34.330
- Do I love Internal Affairs director,

00:01:34.330 --> 00:01:36.720
Sassy Malone, whose primary
character traits are that

00:01:36.720 --> 00:01:39.360
she hates bras and loves cold rooms?

00:01:39.360 --> 00:01:40.193
Not especially.

00:01:40.193 --> 00:01:41.960
It feels gratuitous and male-gaze-y.

00:01:41.960 --> 00:01:43.700
But hey, pays for my expensive habit

00:01:43.700 --> 00:01:45.620
of having a mortgage
in Southern California.

00:01:45.620 --> 00:01:46.453
- You don't have to go.

00:01:46.453 --> 00:01:47.910
We could hang out.

00:01:47.910 --> 00:01:49.090
I'm sure you don't wanna be

00:01:49.090 --> 00:01:50.780
all alone in the house by yourself.

00:01:50.780 --> 00:01:51.970
- No, I love being alone.

00:01:51.970 --> 00:01:53.414
I wish I were alone right now.

00:01:53.414 --> 00:01:54.352
(door clacks)

00:01:54.352 --> 00:01:55.633
(sighs)

00:01:55.633 --> 00:01:58.466
(sorrowful music)

00:02:04.009 --> 00:02:06.176
(gulping)

00:02:08.898 --> 00:02:10.898
(sighs)

00:02:15.582 --> 00:02:16.832
- [BoJack] Huh.

00:02:17.871 --> 00:02:19.730
(phone ringing)

00:02:19.730 --> 00:02:20.608
(groans)

00:02:20.608 --> 00:02:21.900
- [Hollyhock] BoJack?

00:02:21.900 --> 00:02:22.923
Why are you up?

00:02:22.923 --> 00:02:24.760
- I could ask you the same question.

00:02:24.760 --> 00:02:25.730
What, now that you're in college,

00:02:25.730 --> 00:02:27.200
you don't need to sleep anymore?

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:28.490
- No, I was sleeping.

00:02:28.490 --> 00:02:30.120
You called me and woke me up.

00:02:30.120 --> 00:02:31.120
- Oh, right.

00:02:31.120 --> 00:02:32.010
Well, I wanted to let you know

00:02:32.010 --> 00:02:33.660
that I hearted your Instagram photo.

00:02:33.660 --> 00:02:34.580
- Okay.

00:02:34.580 --> 00:02:35.413
Cool.

00:02:35.413 --> 00:02:36.670
- Well, there were 23 other hearts,

00:02:36.670 --> 00:02:38.600
but I don't know if you
know who they're all from.

00:02:38.600 --> 00:02:39.896
But one was from me.

00:02:39.896 --> 00:02:42.150
- Yeah, they let me know.

00:02:42.150 --> 00:02:43.193
- Oh, cool, cool.

00:02:44.080 --> 00:02:45.260
- Okay.

00:02:45.260 --> 00:02:46.860
I'm going back to sleep.

00:02:46.860 --> 00:02:47.983
- Fine, but this phone call does

00:02:47.983 --> 00:02:50.330
not replace our weekly Sunday call, okay?

00:02:50.330 --> 00:02:52.430
- Yeah, I'll talk to you Sunday.

00:02:52.430 --> 00:02:53.358
Afternoon.

00:02:53.358 --> 00:02:55.540
- Yes, good, because I miss you.

00:02:55.540 --> 00:02:56.620
Sorry, that sounded dumb.

00:02:56.620 --> 00:02:59.200
I don't miss you, I'm just bored.

00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:00.320
That also sounded dumb.

00:03:00.320 --> 00:03:02.452
- [Hollyhock] I miss you too, BoJack.

00:03:02.452 --> 00:03:03.570
(phone beeps)

00:03:03.570 --> 00:03:08.240
- My mother is dead and
everything is worse now,

00:03:08.240 --> 00:03:11.130
because now I know I
will never have a mother

00:03:11.130 --> 00:03:12.910
who looks at me from across the room

00:03:12.910 --> 00:03:16.757
and says, "BoJack Horseman, I see you."

00:03:17.830 --> 00:03:19.930
But I guess it's good to know.

00:03:19.930 --> 00:03:23.040
It's good to know that there
is nobody looking out for me,

00:03:23.040 --> 00:03:25.510
that there never was
and there never will be.

00:03:25.510 --> 00:03:26.790
No, it's good to know that I am the

00:03:26.790 --> 00:03:29.050
only one that I can depend on.

00:03:29.050 --> 00:03:31.220
And I know that now, and it's good.

00:03:31.220 --> 00:03:32.260
It's good that I know that.

00:03:32.260 --> 00:03:34.693
So it's good my mother's dead.

00:03:36.001 --> 00:03:37.530
(inhales)

00:03:37.530 --> 00:03:39.680
Well, no point beating a dead horse.

00:03:39.680 --> 00:03:44.070
Beatrice Horseman was born
in 1938 and she died in 2018,

00:03:44.070 --> 00:03:47.223
and I have no idea what she wanted.

00:03:50.140 --> 00:03:52.223
Unless she just wanted what we all want:

00:03:53.170 --> 00:03:54.083
To be seen.

00:03:57.767 --> 00:03:59.850
(creaks)

00:04:03.910 --> 00:04:06.743
(paper crinkling)

00:04:09.197 --> 00:04:10.740
(slurps)

00:04:10.740 --> 00:04:12.890
(blows nose)

00:04:12.890 --> 00:04:14.510
Is this funeral parlor B?

00:04:14.510 --> 00:04:15.343
- Okay.

00:04:15.343 --> 00:04:16.840
Now for the real work to begin.

00:04:16.840 --> 00:04:17.673
- Real what, now?

00:04:17.673 --> 00:04:19.730
- You did the hard part,
admitting you need help.

00:04:19.730 --> 00:04:20.700
- Did I admit that?

00:04:20.700 --> 00:04:23.360
- And now comes the even
harder part, getting the help.

00:04:23.360 --> 00:04:24.730
Let's talk about your mother.

00:04:24.730 --> 00:04:25.563
- You know what?

00:04:25.563 --> 00:04:26.720
This has been great.

00:04:26.720 --> 00:04:28.810
I got what I wanted and
I made so much progress,

00:04:28.810 --> 00:04:30.165
so I think I'm done.

00:04:30.165 --> 00:04:31.269
(Dr. Indira mumbles)
Yes, you did it.

00:04:31.269 --> 00:04:32.480
You changed my stripes.

00:04:32.480 --> 00:04:34.580
Dr. Indira, you're great at your job.

00:04:34.580 --> 00:04:35.511
Goodbye forever.

00:04:35.511 --> 00:04:36.970
(Dr. Indira stutters)
(door slams)

00:04:36.970 --> 00:04:38.871
I went to the room where
they were keeping this stuff.

00:04:38.871 --> 00:04:40.386
(gun fires)
(clangs)

00:04:40.386 --> 00:04:41.219
(dramatic music)

00:04:41.219 --> 00:04:43.110
Only there was no stuff.

00:04:43.110 --> 00:04:43.943
- Oh, my god.

00:04:43.943 --> 00:04:45.130
- There was a girl there.

00:04:45.130 --> 00:04:47.700
She couldn't have been older than 17.

00:04:47.700 --> 00:04:48.630
- Bring in the girl.

00:04:48.630 --> 00:04:49.740
- What?
What is this?

00:04:49.740 --> 00:04:50.573
- Keep going.

00:04:50.573 --> 00:04:52.338
We gotta get this tonight.

00:04:52.338 --> 00:04:53.320
- A girl?

00:04:53.320 --> 00:04:54.800
- [BoJack] They weren't smuggling drugs.

00:04:54.800 --> 00:04:56.810
They were smuggling her.

00:04:56.810 --> 00:04:58.140
- Hey, are you okay?

00:04:58.140 --> 00:04:58.973
- Yeah, I'm fine.

00:04:58.973 --> 00:04:59.806
Just do the scene.

00:04:59.806 --> 00:05:01.220
- [BoJack] I told her
it was going to be okay

00:05:01.220 --> 00:05:02.661
and she kissed me.

00:05:02.661 --> 00:05:03.494
(lips smack)

00:05:03.494 --> 00:05:04.327
- What?

00:05:04.327 --> 00:05:06.080
- What did you do to her, Philbert?

00:05:06.080 --> 00:05:06.913
- Nothing.

00:05:06.913 --> 00:05:07.965
Like I said, she kissed me.

00:05:07.965 --> 00:05:08.798
(lips smack)

00:05:08.798 --> 00:05:09.631
- Kiss her back.

00:05:09.631 --> 00:05:10.690
- What?
- We need to get

00:05:10.690 --> 00:05:11.820
you kissing her back.

00:05:11.820 --> 00:05:13.220
- Kiss me, you idiot.

00:05:13.220 --> 00:05:14.525
- Kiss her.

00:05:14.525 --> 00:05:16.320
(lips smacking)

00:05:16.320 --> 00:05:17.380
- This whole thing is gonna blow.

00:05:17.380 --> 00:05:18.490
We gotta bounce, friend-o.

00:05:18.490 --> 00:05:20.120
- If Fritz hadn't come for you,

00:05:20.120 --> 00:05:21.410
what would you have done with the girl?

00:05:21.410 --> 00:05:23.640
- [BoJack] Part of me is sure
I couldn't go through with it,

00:05:23.640 --> 00:05:25.520
but another part knows that's a lie.

00:05:25.520 --> 00:05:27.240
- We can't just leave her here.

00:05:27.240 --> 00:05:28.570
- Use your brain, Philbert.

00:05:28.570 --> 00:05:30.000
- Malone, you gotta believe me.

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:31.070
I'm a good guy.

00:05:31.070 --> 00:05:33.310
If I'd known she was
there, I never would've.

00:05:33.310 --> 00:05:34.143
- Tell me what happened.

00:05:34.143 --> 00:05:34.976
- I'll be back.

00:05:34.976 --> 00:05:35.809
You wait right here.

00:05:35.809 --> 00:05:36.940
- Come on, lover boy.

00:05:36.940 --> 00:05:38.200
(splashing)

00:05:38.200 --> 00:05:41.710
- You kissed a young girl
and then left her to die.

00:05:41.710 --> 00:05:42.690
- I'm a good guy.

00:05:42.690 --> 00:05:44.300
I didn't know that she was.

00:05:44.300 --> 00:05:46.120
You have to understand, I'm a good guy.

00:05:46.120 --> 00:05:47.210
- She trusted you.

00:05:47.210 --> 00:05:48.470
- How do you make something right

00:05:48.470 --> 00:05:52.410
when you've made it so
wrong you can never go back?

00:05:52.410 --> 00:05:53.973
- How did you come up with all this?

00:05:53.973 --> 00:05:55.640
- It's a story I heard once.

00:05:55.640 --> 00:05:57.640
I just changed all the names.

00:05:57.640 --> 00:06:01.868
- I'll never forget that night
on the U.S.S. New Mexico.

00:06:01.868 --> 00:06:02.701
(intense violin)

00:06:02.701 --> 00:06:04.170
- Why are you telling me all this?

00:06:04.170 --> 00:06:06.800
- It's just good to
have someone to talk to.

00:06:06.800 --> 00:06:08.400
- [Flip] Cut.
(bell rings)

00:06:08.400 --> 00:06:09.233
Amazing.

00:06:09.233 --> 00:06:10.332
I'm a genius.

00:06:10.332 --> 00:06:13.665
(dramatic guitar strum)

00:06:14.630 --> 00:06:16.880
- Hey, why do you have a vodka bottle

00:06:16.880 --> 00:06:18.270
for every day of the week?

00:06:18.270 --> 00:06:19.780
- Oh, that's just my
new system I'm trying.

00:06:19.780 --> 00:06:21.100
I'm down to one bottle a day.

00:06:21.100 --> 00:06:22.580
- Is this like an AA thing?

00:06:22.580 --> 00:06:23.417
- No, I don't need AA.

00:06:23.417 --> 00:06:25.220
Would you get outta there?

00:06:25.220 --> 00:06:26.330
- I want ice cream.

00:06:26.330 --> 00:06:27.163
Gimme your keys.

00:06:27.163 --> 00:06:27.996
- What?
No.

00:06:27.996 --> 00:06:28.829
- Come on.

00:06:28.829 --> 00:06:29.830
Let me drive the Tesla.

00:06:29.830 --> 00:06:31.070
- With your greasy pizza fingers?

00:06:31.070 --> 00:06:31.903
Forget it.

00:06:31.903 --> 00:06:34.616
- Come on.
- Hey!

00:06:34.616 --> 00:06:35.449
(dramatic whoosh)
- Ooh!

00:06:35.449 --> 00:06:36.720
What the hell are these?

00:06:36.720 --> 00:06:37.553
- What?

00:06:37.553 --> 00:06:38.530
Oh, those--
- Why was this

00:06:38.530 --> 00:06:39.470
in your pocket?

00:06:39.470 --> 00:06:40.303
Are these for me?

00:06:40.303 --> 00:06:41.666
- No.
Hollyhock, god, no.

00:06:41.666 --> 00:06:43.640
- Oh, god, did you put this in my pizza?

00:06:43.640 --> 00:06:44.473
- What?

00:06:44.473 --> 00:06:45.550
Of course not.
Hollyhock, no.

00:06:45.550 --> 00:06:46.383
Give me the--

00:06:46.383 --> 00:06:47.560
No!
(garbage disposal rattling)

00:06:47.560 --> 00:06:48.400
- Oops.

00:06:48.400 --> 00:06:50.110
- Hollyhock, those were for my back.

00:06:50.110 --> 00:06:51.450
- Wait, for real?

00:06:51.450 --> 00:06:52.770
- Yes.
- Oh,

00:06:52.770 --> 00:06:54.446
then actually oops.

00:06:54.446 --> 00:06:55.375
(dramatic music)

00:06:55.375 --> 00:06:57.862
(BoJack panting)

00:06:57.862 --> 00:06:59.300
(coughs)

00:06:59.300 --> 00:07:01.110
- There's gotta be
another way to get pills.

00:07:01.110 --> 00:07:02.500
How about calling this Jobie guy?

00:07:02.500 --> 00:07:03.590
He sounds like a druggie.

00:07:03.590 --> 00:07:05.300
- I thought your back hurts.

00:07:05.300 --> 00:07:06.133
- Yeah.

00:07:06.133 --> 00:07:08.220
- How did you lift me over the fence?

00:07:08.220 --> 00:07:09.370
- Well, the adrenaline kicked in--

00:07:09.370 --> 00:07:11.800
- Do you really need these pills?

00:07:11.800 --> 00:07:12.633
- Hollyhock, how many times?

00:07:12.633 --> 00:07:14.470
- I'm just saying, is it at all possible

00:07:14.470 --> 00:07:15.303
that maybe you don't--

00:07:15.303 --> 00:07:16.280
- Okay, you go to college

00:07:16.280 --> 00:07:18.190
and suddenly you're so sophisticated

00:07:18.190 --> 00:07:19.670
and I'm just a dumb junkie,

00:07:19.670 --> 00:07:20.503
is that it?
- What?

00:07:20.503 --> 00:07:21.336
No!

00:07:21.336 --> 00:07:22.169
- You don't understand anything.

00:07:22.169 --> 00:07:24.330
I am in pain--
- No I get that but I--

00:07:24.330 --> 00:07:26.370
All the time, my whole
life and you have no idea.

00:07:26.370 --> 00:07:28.930
So sorry that you had one
bad experience with my mom.

00:07:28.930 --> 00:07:32.708
But I have been in pain my whole life.

00:07:32.708 --> 00:07:36.250
(sigh)
- I think you should take me

00:07:36.250 --> 00:07:37.193
to the airport.

00:07:38.250 --> 00:07:39.083
- Okay.

00:07:41.842 --> 00:07:46.842
(plane engine roars)
(emotional music)

00:07:47.056 --> 00:07:49.889
(seatbelt clicks)

00:07:50.970 --> 00:07:53.338
- So I guess I'll see you later.

00:07:53.338 --> 00:07:55.420
- Hollyhock I'm sorry.

00:07:55.420 --> 00:07:56.520
- Me too.

00:07:56.520 --> 00:07:59.683
- Maybe it's possible that I don't,

00:07:59.683 --> 00:08:03.760
100% need need the pills.

00:08:03.760 --> 00:08:05.339
I thought I did, but yeah.

00:08:05.339 --> 00:08:09.050
So, thank you for caring about me.

00:08:09.050 --> 00:08:10.820
- Are you going to be okay?

00:08:10.820 --> 00:08:11.653
- Yeah.

00:08:11.653 --> 00:08:14.010
- I could take a semester
off if you need someone.

00:08:14.010 --> 00:08:15.220
- No!
God no.

00:08:15.220 --> 00:08:16.680
Stay...

00:08:16.680 --> 00:08:19.340
Stay in school and take your classes

00:08:19.340 --> 00:08:21.950
and kiss boys and do the college thing.

00:08:21.950 --> 00:08:23.060
I'm gonna be fine.

00:08:23.060 --> 00:08:24.530
I get it drugs are bad.

00:08:24.530 --> 00:08:26.200
- Not all drugs.

00:08:26.200 --> 00:08:28.800
Obviously if you get
hurt again and a doctor.

00:08:28.800 --> 00:08:32.350
A real doctor prescribes you
pain killers you can take them.

00:08:32.350 --> 00:08:34.155
But only if you get hurt again.

00:08:34.155 --> 00:08:34.988
- Okay.

00:08:34.988 --> 00:08:35.930
- You promise?

00:08:35.930 --> 00:08:37.650
- Yes, I promise.

00:08:37.650 --> 00:08:38.990
- Okay.

00:08:38.990 --> 00:08:40.458
I love you.

00:08:40.458 --> 00:08:43.420
(inhales)
(grunts)

00:08:43.420 --> 00:08:45.040
Okay,

00:08:45.040 --> 00:08:45.913
bye.

00:08:47.127 --> 00:08:49.627
(doors shuts)

00:08:51.053 --> 00:08:56.053
♪ Silence release me. ♪

00:08:56.154 --> 00:08:58.582
♪ Speaks when I can't. ♪

00:08:58.582 --> 00:09:00.392
(whoosh)

00:09:00.392 --> 00:09:02.559
(exhales)

00:09:12.369 --> 00:09:13.530
- Ugh!

00:09:13.530 --> 00:09:16.613
(vehicles whooshing)

00:09:20.784 --> 00:09:23.034
(groaning)

00:09:24.073 --> 00:09:25.380
(tires squeal)
(horn honks)

00:09:25.380 --> 00:09:27.130
(crash)

00:09:27.130 --> 00:09:29.183
I went to New Mexico to see Charlotte.

00:09:30.250 --> 00:09:31.970
She was married with a daughter.

00:09:31.970 --> 00:09:33.750
But it wasn't like what you're thinking.

00:09:33.750 --> 00:09:36.250
She was 17 which is the
legal age of concent

00:09:36.250 --> 00:09:37.750
in New Mexico and she wasn't drunk so.

00:09:37.750 --> 00:09:38.620
Not that I wanted to.

00:09:38.620 --> 00:09:39.453
I never.

00:09:39.453 --> 00:09:40.286
And I didn't.

00:09:40.286 --> 00:09:41.880
That's the dumbest part of all of this.

00:09:41.880 --> 00:09:43.040
I didn't do anything.

00:09:43.040 --> 00:09:44.770
I mean, the fact that this has turned into

00:09:44.770 --> 00:09:45.650
such a thing for you.

00:09:45.650 --> 00:09:47.015
You know, maybe I didn't tell you because

00:09:47.015 --> 00:09:48.440
there was nothing to tell.

00:09:48.440 --> 00:09:49.440
Did you ever think of that.

00:09:49.440 --> 00:09:51.362
I mean she was my friends
daughter and she wanted it,

00:09:51.362 --> 00:09:52.365
(stutters)
and I was...

00:09:52.365 --> 00:09:53.970
(inhales)
I was in a bad place

00:09:53.970 --> 00:09:55.590
because Charlotte had just...

00:09:55.590 --> 00:09:57.500
So then she came on to my boat,

00:09:57.500 --> 00:09:58.420
Charlotte I mean,

00:09:58.420 --> 00:10:00.370
and she walked in and I
was with her daughter.

00:10:00.370 --> 00:10:02.870
But again nothing had happened yet.

00:10:02.870 --> 00:10:03.703
- Yet?

00:10:03.703 --> 00:10:04.830
- Nothing happened.

00:10:04.830 --> 00:10:06.670
- Goodbye BoJack.
- Dianne no.

00:10:06.670 --> 00:10:07.503
- Ahh!

00:10:07.503 --> 00:10:08.520
- You wanted me to tell you, I told you.

00:10:08.520 --> 00:10:09.500
You know everything.

00:10:09.500 --> 00:10:10.630
- Please let go of me.

00:10:10.630 --> 00:10:11.690
- Dianne please.

00:10:11.690 --> 00:10:12.523
- You're hurting me,

00:10:12.523 --> 00:10:14.582
and I would like you to let go now.

00:10:14.582 --> 00:10:18.398
(BoJack huffs)
(Dianne exhales)

00:10:18.398 --> 00:10:20.648
(cap pops)

00:10:21.938 --> 00:10:24.616
(gulps)

00:10:24.616 --> 00:10:26.949
(sad music)

00:10:29.635 --> 00:10:30.870
- Give me my pills back!

00:10:30.870 --> 00:10:32.210
- No.
- So what happens now?

00:10:32.210 --> 00:10:33.070
- You turn yourself in.

00:10:33.070 --> 00:10:33.903
- Are you kidding?

00:10:33.903 --> 00:10:34.736
- I know there's a good man

00:10:34.736 --> 00:10:36.280
buried in there somewhere Philbert.

00:10:36.280 --> 00:10:37.654
He's the man I fell in love with.

00:10:37.654 --> 00:10:38.950
(dramatic piano)
(violin screech)

00:10:38.950 --> 00:10:39.997
- That man is dead!

00:10:39.997 --> 00:10:40.860
(slam)
(Gina yells)

00:10:40.860 --> 00:10:42.600
Gina, I'm not kidding the pills.

00:10:42.600 --> 00:10:43.433
Now!
(wall smashes)

00:10:43.433 --> 00:10:44.290
- You're out of control.

00:10:44.290 --> 00:10:45.256
- Give them to me!

00:10:45.256 --> 00:10:47.189
(groaning)
(Gina struggling)

00:10:47.189 --> 00:10:48.291
- Stop, let go!
(whack)

00:10:48.291 --> 00:10:49.883
Ahh,
you're hurting me.

00:10:51.742 --> 00:10:53.460
(heavy breathing)

00:10:53.460 --> 00:10:55.110
- [Flip] Okay, cut.

00:10:55.110 --> 00:10:57.190
- BoJack, he said cut.

00:10:57.190 --> 00:10:58.621
- BoJack, buddy?

00:10:58.621 --> 00:10:59.454
- Uh?

00:10:59.454 --> 00:11:02.270
- I think he's really strangling her.

00:11:02.270 --> 00:11:03.820
- What?
Oh no.

00:11:03.820 --> 00:11:05.377
Turn the camera back on.

00:11:05.377 --> 00:11:07.100
(eerie music)
(Gina struggling)

00:11:07.100 --> 00:11:08.280
- Gina, you okay?

00:11:08.280 --> 00:11:09.828
- Okay, that enough.

00:11:09.828 --> 00:11:11.588
(BoJack grunts)
(roars)

00:11:11.588 --> 00:11:14.750
(heavy breathing)

00:11:14.750 --> 00:11:16.310
- What the fuck is wrong with you?

00:11:16.310 --> 00:11:17.216
- Uh.

00:11:17.216 --> 00:11:19.799
(camera flash)

00:11:21.460 --> 00:11:23.060
- Look, you have two options.

00:11:23.060 --> 00:11:25.340
You can go back home and
try to do things your way

00:11:25.340 --> 00:11:27.109
like you've been doing all your life.

00:11:27.109 --> 00:11:30.181
Or you can see what
these guys have to offer.

00:11:30.181 --> 00:11:32.230
(door shuts)

00:11:32.230 --> 00:11:34.830
- I don't understand why
you're being so nice to me.

00:11:34.830 --> 00:11:36.280
After everything you know about me,

00:11:36.280 --> 00:11:37.830
all the shit I put you through.

00:11:38.840 --> 00:11:42.220
- When I was in high school
I had this friend, Abby.

00:11:42.220 --> 00:11:45.200
She was my only friend, and
we did everything together.

00:11:45.200 --> 00:11:47.720
Until she got adopted by the cool kids

00:11:47.720 --> 00:11:49.260
and then she turned on me.

00:11:49.260 --> 00:11:50.530
So fast.

00:11:50.530 --> 00:11:52.900
She used every secret she knew about me,

00:11:52.900 --> 00:11:54.110
every vulnerability.

00:11:54.110 --> 00:11:57.235
She made me miserable my
entire sophomore year.

00:11:57.235 --> 00:12:00.380
But then that summer
when her mom got sick,

00:12:00.380 --> 00:12:02.110
like really sick,

00:12:02.110 --> 00:12:03.590
and all her cool friends were off

00:12:03.590 --> 00:12:05.165
vacationing in Martha's Vineyard.

00:12:05.165 --> 00:12:06.362
I was there for her.

00:12:06.362 --> 00:12:08.110
(puffs cigarette)
- Why?

00:12:08.110 --> 00:12:09.714
- Because I'm an idiot.

00:12:09.714 --> 00:12:12.170
And it was Abby,

00:12:12.170 --> 00:12:16.150
and I hated her, and I
will never forgive her.

00:12:16.150 --> 00:12:19.600
But she needed me and
she was my best friend,

00:12:19.600 --> 00:12:20.453
and I loved her.

00:12:21.400 --> 00:12:24.370
But now, you're here.

00:12:24.370 --> 00:12:26.150
And I hate you.

00:12:26.150 --> 00:12:28.640
But you're my best friend

00:12:28.640 --> 00:12:30.023
and you need me.

00:12:31.066 --> 00:12:33.288
(deep breath)

00:12:33.288 --> 00:12:34.640
You know what you're gonna say?

00:12:34.640 --> 00:12:35.780
You wanna practice?

00:12:35.780 --> 00:12:37.282
- I'm gonna say,

00:12:37.282 --> 00:12:39.770
Hello I am BoJack Horseman.

00:12:39.770 --> 00:12:43.370
Obviously you know who I
am because I'm very famous,

00:12:43.370 --> 00:12:44.620
and also we called ahead.

00:12:45.560 --> 00:12:48.040
And I am here because

00:12:48.040 --> 00:12:48.873
I need help.

00:12:55.550 --> 00:12:57.550
(sighs)

00:13:06.001 --> 00:13:10.918
(door opens)
(door closes)

00:13:16.506 --> 00:13:21.506
(exhales)
(uplifting music)

